==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-cast up one's accounts.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb}}

# To come to an [[accounting]]; to examine and strike the [[balance]] of [[debt]] and [[credit]]; [[reckon]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005 |title=A Theologico-Political Treatise, and a Political Treatise  |author=Benedictus de Spinoza  |page=xviii |ISBN=1596055219 |passage=He was very careful to '''cast up his accounts''' every quarter ; which he did, that he might spend neither more nor less than what he could spend every year.  }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007 |title=Holiness: Its Nature, Hindrances, Difficulties, and Roots  |author= J. C. Ryle |page=121 |ISBN=1598562223 |passage=If a man should '''cast up his accounts''' once a week, or once a month, he may not be able to discern that he doth grow rich, and yet he may grow rich. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008 |title=Devotional Classics of C. H. Spurgeon  |author=Charles Haddon Spurgeon  |page=18 |ISBN=1589601661 |passage=EVERY WISE MERCHANT will occasionally hold a stock-taking, when he will '''cast up his accounts''', examine what he has on hand, and ascertain decisively whether his trade is prosperous or declining. }}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|archaic}} To [[vomit]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1854|title=The Works of Francis Rabelais - Volume 1  |author=François Rabelais, ‎Jacob Le Duchat, John Ozell  |page=134 |ISBN= |passage=To '''cast up one's accounts''' upon excessive drinking ; either, says Cotgrave, because in spewing one makes a noise like a fox that barks, or (from the subject to the effect) because the flaying of so unsavoury a beast will make any one spew. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004 |title=Secrets of the Night |author=Jo Beverley  |page= |ISBN=110156489X |passage=A foul taste. Vomit. 'Struth! Embarrassing memory flooded back. He'd '''cast up his accounts''' in front of a woman. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|title=Just a Dream |author=Heather Boyd -   |page= |ISBN=0992486319 |passage=As he handed the tray over, he heard the knocker echo through the house. Thinking it might be Jimmy, he turned back to his father to warn him only to see him reach for the chamber pot and '''cast up his accounts'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015 |title=If the Viscount Falls  |author=Sabrina Jeffries  |page=20 |ISBN=1476786135 |passage=She was about to be sick right here in front of them all. That would be the worst humiliation imaginable. Mustn't '''cast up my accounts''', mustn't '''cast up my accounts'''.  }}

